 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. Same to you. How are you? Cleaning them with toothpick on a resticked box helps with the worst of the stiffness. Then a little bit of pressure with toothpaste helps make them bounce again. That's too long. A few hours is about the limit before they start growing mold. A little bit of wrist motion gets them moving again. You can also cut off the stiffest ones and start fresh. Then keep them as fresh as possible and swap them every few months. Cleaning them only makes them worse after a while.",
